Fall back to XDG_SESSION_TYPE when logind cannot attribute the peer.

oo7-daemon picks between the GNOME prompter (org.gnome.keyring.SystemPrompter)
and a CLI prompter from the *calling client's* session type, which it resolves
with logind's GetSessionByPID (upstream 9f4de634, fixing oo7#530 -- it replaced
an earlier check of the daemon's own DISPLAY/WAYLAND_DISPLAY environment).

That lookup answers "PID does not belong to any known session" for every
graphical client on a systemd-managed session. The login session's cgroup
(session-N.scope) holds only the session leader; the compositor and everything
it launches are user units under user@<uid>.service:

  $ loginctl show-session 8 -p Scope -p Type
  Scope=session-8.scope
  Type=wayland
  $ cat /proc/$(pgrep -x niri)/cgroup
  0::/user.slice/user-1000.slice/user@1000.service/session.slice/niri.service
  $ busctl --system call org.freedesktop.login1 /org/freedesktop/login1 \
      org.freedesktop.login1.Manager GetSessionByPID u $(pgrep -x niri)
  Call failed: PID 39347 does not belong to any known session

Verified on a booted krytis system: the lookup succeeds only for PIDs inside
session-8.scope (greetd's session worker -> "wayland") and fails for niri,
noctalia and oo7-daemon alike. SessionType then falls to Unspecified, which is
not graphical, so every libsecret caller is routed to the CLI prompter and
fails with:

  CLI prompter failed: NameHasNoOwner: Name
  "org.freedesktop.secrets.CliPrompter" does not exist

krytis ships no oo7-cli, so nothing ever owns that name. This is krytis#588
surviving its own upstream fix by a different route.

XDG_SESSION_TYPE is set by pam_systemd at session open and inherited by the
systemd user manager, so oo7-daemon carries it (=wayland, alongside
XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=niri) even when no display variable and no resolvable peer
session exists. Consulting it only when the logind lookup fails preserves the
upstream behaviour wherever it works -- a peer in a real tty session scope
still resolves to Tty and still gets the CLI prompter -- and answers the same
question from the daemon's own session otherwise.

Upstream: https://github.com/linux-credentials/oo7/issues/530 -- closed by
9f4de634 on 2026-08-15. The fix is sound for D-Bus-activated daemons on
sessions where clients sit in the session scope, but not for systemd-managed
sessions; the original reporter's GNOME OS setup is likely also still affected.
Tracked downstream as starlit-os/krytis#588. Drop this patch once upstream
handles an unresolvable peer session; reporting it upstream needs an explicit
go-ahead per AGENTS.md's Upstream Gate.
diff --git a/server/src/service/mod.rs b/server/src/service/mod.rs
index 87407d2..ae38527 100644
--- a/server/src/service/mod.rs
+++ b/server/src/service/mod.rs
@@ -136,7 +136,7 @@ impl Service {
                 .to_owned();
             let session_type = SessionType::from_logind(pid)
                 .await
-                .unwrap_or(SessionType::Unspecified);
+                .unwrap_or_else(SessionType::from_env);
             Some(PeerInfo::new(pid, name, session_type))
         }
         .await;
diff --git a/server/src/session.rs b/server/src/session.rs
index e7ec180..4744c22 100644
--- a/server/src/session.rs
+++ b/server/src/session.rs
@@ -49,6 +49,23 @@ impl SessionType {
             _ => Self::Unspecified,
         })
     }
+
+    /// Fallback for peers that logind cannot attribute to a session.
+    ///
+    /// A systemd-managed desktop runs the compositor and its clients as user
+    /// units under `user@<uid>.service`, which is outside the login session's
+    /// own cgroup, so `GetSessionByPID` answers `NoSessionForPID` for every
+    /// graphical client. `XDG_SESSION_TYPE` is set by pam_systemd at session
+    /// open and is inherited by the user manager, so it still describes the
+    /// session this daemon belongs to.
+    pub fn from_env() -> Self {
+        match std::env::var("XDG_SESSION_TYPE").as_deref() {
+            Ok("x11") => Self::X11,
+            Ok("wayland") => Self::Wayland,
+            Ok("tty") => Self::Tty,
+            _ => Self::Unspecified,
+        }
+    }
 }
 
